{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792491653,"nonce":"tlB6m8fccSofF3ztRnhmglNSCRg=","title":"Compiler: share tagged-union layout and caller-owned native return storage","message":"Tagged union storage currently disagrees across the interpreter, Cranelift and LLVM. Native operations assume payload offset four regardless of tag/payload alignment; LLVM reserves a fixed twelve-byte payload, interpreter union instructions are absent, ABI classification omits union pointer passing and caller-owned return storage, and LLVM promotion rejects all union signatures.\n\nEstablish common size/alignment/payload offsets, lower construction/tag/payload operations consistently, preserve value copies through loads and independent return destinations, and test interpreter-first and mixed native promotions. This is a prerequisite for TypeScript scalar unions; do not add a frontend heap-box workaround.\n\nParent: 6875fc2949f83d682861ecab814e0ff82c824f5990620b0d64ca0340ebb026e5","files":null}]}